#### 5.3.2. Maximum Coverage complements Minimum Coverage

A comparison between Minimum Coverage and Maximum Coverage reveals complementary behavior. Minimum Coverage gap ratio is positively correlated with the number of leaf tasks and maximum task degree kTk\_{T}, and negatively correlated with the number of leaf people and kPk\_{P}. Maximum Coverage, on the other hand, exhibits the opposite pattern: its error is positively correlated with kPk\_{P} and the number of leaf people, and negatively correlated with kTk\_{T} and the number of leaf tasks.

